<title>THAILAND: Hipro Electronics to debut on Thai bourse.</title>
<headline>Hipro Electronics to debut on Thai bourse.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hipro Electronics Plc, producer of power component units for Compaq and Dell computers, debuts on the Stock Exchange of Thailand on Friday.</p>
<p>Hipro recently floated 5.4 million of its 27 million shares at an initial public offer of 32 baht underwritten by Jardine Fleming Thanakom Securities Plc.</p>
<p>Hipro's Taiwanese major shareholders retained a 35 percent stake in the company after it went public.</p>
<p>Hipro, whose shares carry a price/earnings ratio of 8.7 times at its public offer, said it expects to earn 1.6 billion baht ($64 million) revenue this year.</p>
<p>(US$1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-2529950-3</p>
